import shapes.dl
import clipping.dl

to draw UI text field {a pointer to UI layout:layout} in {UI bounds:box} focused {boolean:focused} in {a pointer to UI view:view} on {UI frame:frame}:
    set value to the UI value for (layout's node) in (view's instance)
    set border to view's theme's outline
    if (focused and view's keyboard focus) or (layout's hover > 0.0):
        set border to view's theme's accent
    draw a rounded UI box box with radius 8.0 in border on frame
    draw a rounded UI box (UI box at (box's x + 1.0) (box's y + 1.0) sized (box's width - 2.0) (box's height - 2.0)) with radius 7.0 in (view's theme's surface) on frame
    set clip to UI box at (box's x + 10.0) (box's y + 3.0) sized (box's width - 20.0) (box's height - 6.0)
    set saved to a UI clip restricted to clip in view on frame
    set limit to the maximum of 0.0 and ((the width of (value's text) using (view's typeface)) - (clip's width - 2.0))
    set layout's scroll position to the minimum of limit and (layout's scroll position)
    set caret to view's selection's caret run
    if caret != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text run):
        if caret's element = layout's node:
            synchronize editable UI text caret in view
            set offset to the width of (the UI text prefix of (value's text) ending at (view's selection's caret)) using (view's typeface)
            set layout's scroll position to the minimum of (layout's scroll position) and offset
            set layout's scroll position to the maximum of (layout's scroll position) and (offset - (clip's width - 2.0))
    set view's text element to layout's node
    set view's selectable to true
    draw UI text (value's text) at (clip's x - layout's scroll position) (box's y + (((box's height + view's typeface's size) / 2.0) - 2.0)) with (view's typeface) in (view's theme's text) on frame
    if focused and view's keyboard focus:
        if view's selection's caret run != view's last text:
            set view's selection's anchor run to view's last text
            set view's selection's caret run to view's last text
            set view's selection's anchor to value's text's length
            set view's selection's caret to value's text's length
            set view's damaged to true
    if (view's selection's caret run = view's last text) and (view's selection's composition's length > 0):
        set offset to the width of (the UI text prefix of (value's text) ending at (view's selection's caret)) using (view's typeface)
        set view's selectable to false
        set left to (clip's x - layout's scroll position) + offset
        set baseline to box's y + ((box's height + view's typeface's size) / 2.0 - 2.0)
        draw UI text (view's selection's composition) at left baseline with (view's typeface) in (view's theme's accent) on frame
        draw a rectangle at x left and y (baseline + 3.0) with width (the width of (view's selection's composition) using (view's typeface)) and height 1.0 in color red 60, green 100 and blue 190 in frame
    set view's text element to @intrinsic("construct", UI reference)
    set view's selectable to false
    restore UI clip saved in view on frame
